.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
RAM‑based backend for shared device buffers\&. 

\fBRamSharedBackend\fP is the simplest backend in \fBSystemEx\fP\&. It stores buffer data directly in managed RAM and exposes it to native kernels by pinning the underlying \fRbyte[]\fP and providing an unmanaged pointer via \fBUnmanagedObject\fP\&. 

.PP
This backend is primarily used for: 
.PD 0
.IP "\(bu" 2
Testing native kernels without GPU or hardware devices 
.IP "\(bu" 2
Debugging compute logic in a safe environment 
.IP "\(bu" 2
Providing a fallback backend for platforms without specialized hardware 
.PP

.PP
The backend implements the \fBIDeviceSharedBackend\fP interface, allowing \fBSystemEx\fP to treat RAM buffers exactly like hardware buffers\&. This makes native kernel execution backend‑agnostic: 
.br
 kernels do not care whether the memory comes from RAM, GPU, or another device\&. 
.PP
